## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a privacy-aware OTCA telemetry path at scale with per-tenant residency and multi-region replication.

## Key Concepts
- OTLP, OpenTelemetry Collector
- Kafka/Pulsar topology
- Tenant isolation & PII redaction
- Region-local immutable storage & cross-region replication
- SLA-driven sampling & drift testing

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-processor to redact PII in OTEL attributes
class RedactProcessor {
  process(span) {
    const redacted = ['cardNumber','email','ip'];
    redacted.forEach(k => {
      if (span.attributes[k]) span.attributes[k] = 'REDACTED';
    });
    return span;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate privacy compliance across regions?
- How would you monitor cross-region replication lag and SLA breaches?

## Why This Is Asked
Evaluates designing an OTCA telemetry path for a real-time chat app with multi-region tenants, focusing on privacy at ingestion, data residency, and practical streaming topology.

## Key Concepts
- OTCA tenancy and data residency
- Chat-event schema (message_sent, typing events, read_receipt)
- Privacy at ingestion: redaction and hashing
- Idempotent deduplication and per-tenant rate limits
- Streaming: edge gateway, regional Kafka, Parquet on S3 with tenant/date partitions

## Code Example
```javascript
function redactEvent(e){
  const copy = { ...e };
  copy.user_id_hash = hash(copy.user_id_hash);
  delete copy.personal_message;
  return copy;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you verify privacy guarantees across tenants during retention cycles?
- What metrics would you surface to validate QoS and latency under load?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design cross-region data marketplaces under OTCA governance, including residency enforcement, DP budgeting, and auditability.

## Key Concepts

- Data marketplace catalog and policy engine
- Per-tenant residency and epsilon accounting
- Region-scoped streaming and cross-region aggregation
- Immutable audit logs and billing

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo policy evaluation
function evaluateAccess(user, dataset) {
  if (!dataset.policies.includes(user.role)) return false;
  if (Date.now() < dataset.validFrom || Date.now() > dataset.validUntil) return false;
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you revoke access and re-compute epsilon budgets in real time?
- How to test utility loss under bursts and evolving policies?

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates the ability to design governance-focused OTCA telemetry with immutability, privacy controls, and multi-tenant residency, along with a concrete testing plan.

## Key Concepts
- OTCA governance events and immutable auditing
- Per-tenant residency and PII redaction
- Policy engine for retention, privacy, and drift checks
- Streaming topology: client → edge gateway → regional Kafka → central store
- Testing strategy covering privacy, latency, drift, and auditability

## Code Example
```typescript
type GovernanceEvent = {
  tenant_id: string;
  region: string;
  timestamp: string;
  governance_event_type: 'policy_update' | 'quota_violation' | 'model_swap' | 'audit';
  model_id: string;
  policy_version: string;
  user_id_hash: string;
  latency_ms: number;
  action_taken: string;
  audit_id: string;
};

interface TelemetryPipeline {
  ingest(event: GovernanceEvent): Promise<void>;
  enforcePolicy(event: GovernanceEvent): GovernanceEvent;
  route(tenantId: string, region: string): void;
}
```
